# 03 — CLI Execution, Evidence, Boundaries & Review

<!-- GEN: Why: real CLI commands, proof that the new test ran, explicit boundaries, and unified BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR review grading turn test runs into trustworthy evidence. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

Rules **U12**, **U13**, and **U14**.

---

## 1. CLI Commands & Proving the New Test Ran (`U12`)

Every command is binary (`exit 0` = `PASS`, `exit != 0` = `FAIL`):

| Step | Command | What to Verify in Output |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Focused Red Run** | `{{focused_test_cmd}}` | Exits non-zero on the expected assertion failure (not an import/setup error) |
| **2. Focused Green Run** | `{{focused_test_cmd}}` | Exits `0`; verbose output lists the exact new test name as `PASSED` |
| **3. Module Suite** | `{{module_test_cmd}}` | Total passed count increased by the number of added tests; `0 skipped` |
| **4. Full Unit Suite** | `{{full_test_cmd}}` | Entire unit suite passes with deterministic ordering |
| **5. Static Checks on Tests** | `{{test_lint_cmd}}` | Formatter, linter, and type checker pass on `test` files (`exit 0`) |

---

## 2. Red-to-Green Evidence Rows & Result Triaging (`U12`, `U14`)

Record both Red and Green runs in the hand-off (`work-item-contract` `references/handoff-and-status.md` §4, `evidence-standard`):

| Claim | Command (+cwd) | Revision | Exit Code | Key Output | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Task X.Y red: <behavior> not yet enforced` | `{{focused_test_cmd}}` | `<sha>` | `1` | `<expected assertion failure>` | `FAIL` (expected red) |
| `Task X.Y green: <behavior> verified` | `{{focused_test_cmd}}` | `<sha>` | `0` | `1 passed` | `PASS` |

Compare actual output against the task's **Expected** outcome (`MATCH` / `CODE_WRONG` / `PLAN_WRONG`). Non-executed checks must be reported as `NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, or `UNVERIFIED` — never `PASS`.

---

## 3. Unit Test Boundaries (`U13`)

Always state what unit tests covered and what remains for downstream verification:

| Verification Target | Proven By | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| Pure domain rules, use cases/services, schemas/mappers, state transitions, HTTP/adapter error mapping | **Developer Unit Tests** (this skill) | Code Writer |
| Real database queries, constraints, migrations, transactions, live API contracts, E2E flows | **Integration / Acceptance Verification** (`{{verification_link}}`, `quality-acceptance`) | Test Runner (or Code Writer when assigned an integration task) |

---

## 4. Review Severity (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`)

Code Reviewers grade unit tests on the unified 3-tier scale (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md` §2):

| Severity | Finding | Review Verdict Impact |
|---|---|---|
| `BLOCKER` | Any unit test or static check `FAIL`s; new test not collected or skipped (`U12`); bug/finding fix lacks red-to-green regression test (`U3`); subject under test mocked (`U5`); authorization/security guard mocked away (`U6`); existing test edited/weakened to pass | `CHANGES_REQUESTED` |
| `MAJOR` | Missing required Pass/Default, handled Fail, or Empty/Edge case (`U2`); live network/DB/clock in unit test (`U4`, `U7`); tautological or weak assertion (`U8`); test path or setup violates workspace convention (`U10`, `U11`) | Must be fixed in the same phase scope |
| `MINOR` | Minor test naming improvement, AAA formatting, or local builder extraction (`U9`) | Optional (never blocks approval) |

